Correction: the claim that this fixed "any offline launch" is wrong. The URL
is a hardcoded string in uv.cmd, so it costs nothing to have and is present
offline; only a download needs the network. The old code failed on exactly one
combination, checksums set with no URL, which no caller in this repo produces.
It surfaced as a test failure under a bare `uv run pytest`, where the launcher's
TOOL_URL_* are absent, and the real defect was that inherited environment in
the test rather than the wrapper. See 295ca45.

Kept because it is harmless and matches tool-wrapper.sh, which has always
checked the cache before requiring a URL.
